The pinned original source and its exact license text are preserved here.
core/src/sodium_cache.rs ports its reusable twenty-cubed neighborhood, flat
index, zero sentinel, lazy sampling and per-section reset lifecycle to Rust.
The adaptation packs the client's physical/render block states and native
light channels together in safe Cell storage, checks coordinates and retains
its existing AO, emission, fluid, geometry and vertex ABI behavior.

At the pinned commit, BlockRenderCache.init resets ArrayLightDataCache to the
section origin before LevelSlice.copyData. LightDataAccess.compute packs native
light and occlusion data once; smooth and flat light pipelines reuse those
samples. This port applies that cache lifecycle to the browser client's WASM
mesher. Its registry and light lookup remain the client's native data format;
it does not import JVM or Fabric dependencies.
